"Brannagh's grandmother told her the crossroads shrine was the Wayfarer's, who keeps the wandering."
"Brannagh remembers the tale that the Wayfarer would one day send a daughter out of the stone."
"A red-haired stranger from the shrine would make Brannagh think of that tale at once."
"The two blight-bitten townsfolk are the smith Garrod and the weaver's boy Tam; both will sicken."
